xnu 0495: run the first wlan_en cycle without a load

Measured 2026-11-27: `0494` removes the pre-BHI MHI context and the PBL still
stops at `0xef0a0111` with `BHI_STATUS=0`. The 7a port's resolved wall is the
chip's own boot state: its PBL leaves `pbl_auth.c` only when the AoC has
bootstrapped the chip before `WLAN_EN` rises. Stock never loads on the first
`WLAN_EN` cycle either: cnss2 powers and enumerates once, drops `WLAN_EN` with
the buck held, and loads on the second rise, state the WLAON domain keeps
across the cycle. Every load here has been the first one. Pulse `WLAN_EN` and
drop it before the link trains, so the doorbell lands in a PBL that has
already run once.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
@@ -548,6 +548,28 @@
 	delay(1000);
 	delay(3000);
 	wifi_xo_set(0);
+	/*
+	 * Stock never loads the first WLAN_EN cycle. cnss2 powers the chip,
+	 * enumerates it, drops WLAN_EN with the buck held, and does the real
+	 * BHI load on the second rise; the WLAON domain keeps state across
+	 * that cycle. Every load here has been the first one since power-on,
+	 * which is the state the 7a port found on the wrong side of
+	 * pbl_auth.c until its AoC was up. Run the same idle first cycle
+	 * before the link trains: one pulse to let the PBL run and latch,
+	 * a low gap, then the pulse that will get the doorbell.
+	 */
+	delay(50000);
+	wifi_pin_set(wifi_wlan_en_page, mondrian_tlmm_cfg(WIFI_TLMM_FUNC_GPIO,
+	    WIFI_TLMM_PULL_DOWN, WIFI_TLMM_DRIVE_2MA, 1), 0);
+	delay(100000);
+	wifi_log("WLAN pre-cycle rise/fall/rise");
+	wifi_xo_set(1);
+	delay(200);
+	wifi_pin_set(wifi_wlan_en_page, mondrian_tlmm_cfg(WIFI_TLMM_FUNC_GPIO,
+	    WIFI_TLMM_PULL_UP, WIFI_TLMM_DRIVE_16MA, 1), 1);
+	delay(1000);
+	delay(3000);
+	wifi_xo_set(0);
 	delay(60000);
 	wifi_log("WLAN enable complete");
 }
